# NOTE: .gitignore does NOT support trailing comments on a pattern line.
# "cache/    # some note" is parsed as the literal pattern
# "cache/    # some note" and matches nothing. Every comment below is therefore
# on its own line. Verify any change with:
#     git check-ignore -v <path>

# --- Data and derived biometric artefacts: never committed ---
# DAiSEE is licence-restricted (per-user registration) and is video of
# identifiable people. Neither it nor anything derived from the faces belongs
# in this repository.
Datasets/
data/DAiSEE*/

# Face crops (JPEG), landmark coordinates, head pose, and ViT embeddings.
cache/

# Third-party MediaPipe binaries; scripts/fetch_models.py refetches them.
models/*.tflite
models/*.task

# --- Large binaries ---
checkpoints/
*.pt
*.pth
*.onnx

# --- Environment ---
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# --- Logs ---
# Run logs are regenerable and noisy; the training histories that back the
# reported numbers are kept (see the negations below).
logs/*
!logs/.gitkeep
!logs/sampling_stdout.txt
# Every per-epoch training history is kept: these back the reported curves and
# the learned-weight trajectories. Their columns are aggregate only -- epoch,
# losses, accuracies, F1s, learning rates, the five MRS weights -- with no clip
# id, subject id or label value, so they redistribute nothing from DAiSEE.
!logs/training_history_*.csv

# --- Artifacts ---
# Results, reports and plots ARE committed. Face imagery is not.
artifacts/face_crop_preview.png
artifacts/mrs_extremes.png

# Per-clip prediction dumps pair a DAiSEE clip id with its ground-truth
# engagement label, which redistributes dataset labels. Aggregate metrics and
# confusion matrices are committed; these row-level files are not.
artifacts/per_clip_predictions_*.json

# Worked examples from scripts/explain_finetuned.py: frames showing identifiable
# DAiSEE participants, plus clip ids paired with their labels. They stay on the
# machine that ran the model.
artifacts/examples_*/

# Per-run sweep reports; the aggregated JSON in ablation_results.json /
# sampling_experiment.json already contains every number they hold.
artifacts/classification_report_T*_test.txt
artifacts/test_metrics_T*_test.json

# --- OS ---
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store
desktop.ini
